The `immergas_nasa` ESPHome component was written from scratch. Protocol facts (frame layout, CRC,
message types, enums, read/response behaviour, message meanings and scaling) were cross-checked
against the following MIT-licensed projects, which are gratefully acknowledged:

- SamsungNASA - Copyright (c) 2025 Németh Bálint (Aranyalma2) - MIT
  https://github.com/Aranyalma2/SamsungNASA
- pysamsungnasa - pantherale0 - MIT
  https://github.com/pantherale0/pysamsungnasa
  (enum values for 0x4001 / 0x4066 / 0x8001 / 0x8003 / 0x8061, indoor error code list)
- esphome_samsung_hvac_bus - Copyright (c) 2024 Ömer Faruk ARAN and contributors - MIT
  https://github.com/omerfaruk-aran/esphome_samsung_hvac_bus
  (idea: transmit only after a quiet period on the bus)

No code from projects without a license or under GPL was used.

Outdoor-unit error descriptions are written in our own words based on the Samsung EHS service
documentation. Values, scaling and meanings specific to the Immergas Magis Combo / Audax Pro V2 come
from the author's own live captures of the F1/F2 bus, cross-checked against the Immergas D+/D- and
T-/T+ (BMS) buses.

